{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791586319,"nonce":"MX4oOZ6x1q5zijH043PWUiEO+O0=","message":"Re-measured with blinc_abi 11283dc (narrowed restyle; inline values as text) in 2037761. CI pins 11283dc and is green.\n\n**Benchmark fix first.** The frame benchmark's paint edits were mostly no-ops: each cell is touched every tenth frame, and its colour was picked by frame parity, so it was set to the colour it already had. With the old full-subtree restyle that did not show; with the narrowed one it did (19 nodes a frame). Cells now get a colour they did not hold (by floor(n/10) parity), so every frame makes 300 real inline changes. The benchmark also reports nodes restyled per frame.\n\n**Measured** (2026-10-09 about 23:45 BST, Node 24.2.0, M-series Mac, release addons, load average 20-30 from other work; benchmarks/host-frame.mjs, 6,031 nodes, each frame 300 inline background edits, 300 text edits, 30 cell moves between rows, then layout; \"old\" is 123f1f5 before CSS, built in a worktree; old and new run alternately, three rounds; median ms per frame; per-method ms are averages over all 36 frames):\n- old: 58.6, 57.2, 56.2 ms. compute 66-72.\n- new, as benchmarked (edits and moves): 74.0, 73.8, 73.1 ms. 6,030 nodes restyled a frame; cssRestyle 16.1-16.7 ms; compute 68-71.\n- new, the same frame without the 30 moves: 60.9, 60.0, 61.1 ms. 300 nodes restyled a frame (exactly the edited cells); cssRestyle 3.1-3.3 ms.\n\nSo inline edits now cost about 3 ms per 300 nodes. The rest comes from the moves: inserting a child marks the old and the new row as moved (Styles::moved, which the addon calls for a parent that gained or lost a child), and a moved node restyles its subtree and every later sibling's, so 30 moves among 30 rows reach the whole tree.\n\n**Where the 16 ms goes** (macOS sample, 6 s, 473 samples in cssRestyle; self time with allocation and hashing attributed to the caller):\n- Walking the tree, about 40%: LayoutContext::children, through child_list and blinc_layout's LayoutTree::children, which allocates a Vec per call and maps every taffy NodeId back through a SipHash HashMap (LayoutTree8children 82, LayoutContext::children 46, child_list 16 samples of allocation and hashing). It is called for the reach phase and again for the parents-first order.\n- The reach closure building the to-do HashSet of 6,030 raw ids (SipHash inserts): about 80.\n- Restyle's own allocation and hashing (dependents and depends_on maps, applied list): about 62.\n- Cloning the parent's Computed for each child: about 45.\n- Cascade::style (matching) itself: about 36. layout_writes and LayoutContext::apply: about 25.\nMatching is a small part. Not changing src/css; suggestions for its owner: walk the tree once with a reused child buffer (or a children iterator that does not allocate), a faster hasher (FxHash) for node-keyed maps and sets, borrowing rather than cloning the parent's Computed, and for a moved child, restyling the parent's children (for structural selectors) rather than the parent's whole subtree when no rule tests siblings beyond the node itself.","files":null}]}